📱 Adaptive Android Application – ListView & ImageView

A simple Adaptive Android Application developed using Kotlin that demonstrates the use of ListView and ImageView to display a list of students with their profile images and course information.

📌 Project Overview

This application was developed as part of the Mobile Application Development lab. It demonstrates how to create a dynamic student list using Android's ListView and display images using ImageView.

The user can view multiple student details in a scrollable list and tap on a student to receive a selection message.

✨ Features
📋 Student list using ListView
🖼️ Student images using ImageView
👤 Displays student name
🎓 Displays course information
👆 Clickable list items
🔔 Toast message when a student is selected
📱 Adaptive layout for different Android screen sizes
🗂️ Images stored in the drawable resource folder
💻 UI created programmatically using Kotlin
🛠️ Technologies Used
Language: Kotlin
IDE: Android Studio
Platform: Android
Minimum SDK: 24
Target SDK: 37
UI Components: ListView, ImageView, TextView, LinearLayout
Build System: Gradle
Version Control: Git & GitHub
